gpsd_shutdown() no longer cleared gpsd_running (since Leste's fb6729a,
which started location-daemon over D-Bus). Once positioning had run,
start_internal() returned at once: location_gpsd_control_start() after
location_gpsd_control_stop() did nothing (no gpsd_running signal, no start
of location-daemon), and the restart after a change of the method, the
settings or MCE's device mode was none. The same fix is in Leste's
liblocation (patches/fixes/liblocation.patch).

--- a/src/location-gpsd-control.c
+++ b/src/location-gpsd-control.c
@@ -141,6 +141,10 @@
 		g_object_unref(p->location_daemon_proxy);
 		p->location_daemon_proxy = NULL;
 	}
+	/* positioning ended: the next start_internal() starts it again (a
+	 * restart after a change of method or settings, start() after
+	 * stop(), with its gpsd_running signal) */
+	p->gpsd_running = FALSE;
 }
 
 int gpsd_start(LocationGPSDControl *control)
